      "content": "It is deeply understandable to feel that profound despair when the world's heavy problems feel overwhelming and unstoppable.\n\nPlease consider that feeling doom is a powerful and common emotional response to the scale of the crisis, but it is not the final word on hope or meaning.\n\nFocusing your attention can help you carve out a meaningful space, such as through direct, local action or deep, immediate self- care.\n\nThere is still profound purpose to be found in the here and now, and in the ways we choose to treat each other and the immediate world around us.",
